diff --git a/research/sources.md b/research/sources.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a43e8fa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/sources.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Compatibility research consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-13.
+
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — confirmed that VCF Operations precedes the 9.1 lifecycle workflows, that VCF Management Services is mandatory, and that the license server is required.
+- **Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html — confirmed the core SDDC order SDDC Manager, NSX, vCenter, witness, then ESXi, and the Aria Suite Lifecycle bridge-patch dependency.
+- **Disabling Witness Host Upgrade in VCF SDDC Manager and vCenter** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/426286/disabling-witness-host-upgrade-in-vcf-sd.html — confirmed that SDDC Manager orchestrates virtual witness remediation and that witness readiness can block data-host remediation in VCF 9.1.
+- **Could not retrieve binary for component during Deploy and Validate in VCF 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/436258/could-not-retrieve-binary-for-component.html — confirmed the active 9.1 GA build targets for SDDC Manager (25371088), NSX (25318225), and vCenter (25370922).
+- **vSAN Stretched Cluster Bandwidth Sizing: Recommendations for vSAN in VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1** — https://www.vmware.com/docs/vmw-vsan-stretched-cluster-bandwidth-sizing — confirmed two data fault domains plus a third witness fault domain, at least 10 Gbps and under 5 ms RTT between data sites, and under 200 ms RTT to a witness for this host count.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation API Specifications, tag 9.1.0.0** — https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/tree/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer — confirmed the installer `SddcSpec` field names and nested VCF Installer models used by the PowerCLI constructors.
